# SL₂(ℤ)-invariance of E₄³/Δ

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.E4_cube_div_discriminant_smul`
(`c0acef28-60a7-5603-ba6b-5202f4dad3b3`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `677c6c79-20ba-5ac7-afee-62a70e6c35ad`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

For every $\gamma$ in the special linear group $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ (Mathlib's
`Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℤ`) and every point $\tau$ of the upper half-plane
$\mathfrak{H}$, the complex number $E_4(\gamma\cdot\tau)^3/\Delta(\gamma\cdot\tau)$ equals
$E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$. Here $E_4$ is Mathlib's normalised weight-$4$ Eisenstein series
`ModularForm.E₄` for the full modular group, $\Delta$ is the modular discriminant
`ModularForm.discriminant`, $\gamma\cdot\tau$ is the usual action of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ on
$\mathfrak{H}$ by fractional linear transformations, and the cube and the quotient are taken in
$\mathbb{C}$. No non-vanishing hypothesis on $\Delta$ enters: with Lean's convention $x/0 = 0$ the
asserted identity holds as stated, so this is exactly the invariance of the function $\tau \mapsto
E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$ on $\mathfrak{H}$ under the full modular group, with no claim that the
common value is finite or that it computes the $j$-invariant up to a constant.

This is the $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$-invariance of the level-one modular function $E_4^3/\Delta$,
i.e. of the modular invariant $j$ up to normalisation. It is used in the treatment of the modular
curve: stabiliser and ramification computations for complex points, membership statements for
algebras generated by $j$ and $q$, and the Fricke involution on $\Gamma_0$-invariant expansions.

